description.narrative:
CRC operational priorities
In 2026, the ICRC’s main priorities in this context will be to:
increase respect for IHL among the authorities and weapon bearers, emphasizing the need to ensure protection for civilians; broaden acceptance for its neutral, impartial and independent humanitarian action, with a view to securing safe access to conflict-affected communities;
address the protection-related concerns of IDPs, refugees and other civilians affected by conflict, including their need for family contact or news of their missing relatives; respond to their urgent needs during emergencies;
support the local authorities and service providers in ensuring the sustainable provision of essential services, particularly health care, water and sanitation; raise awareness, among communities and the authorities, of the effects of weapon contamination;
seek access to all detainees within its purview; support the authorities in ensuring that the treatment and living conditions of detainees meet internationally recognized standards; and
maintain comprehensive support for the Libyan Red Crescent, to strengthen its institutional and operational capacities, and foster coordination with other Movement components in addressing humanitarian needs.
